    "lastCommit": {
      "id": "0033536cee170b95bf2f474b0c24b5bae8b2517b",
      "message": "[ota-hal] OTA-1678: the chase gets harder\n\nItem six (a) of \"fix all existing issues one through six\": the flee\nescalation, on the randoms only.\n\nTHE OWNER'S RULE, IN HIS WORDS\n\"on the randoms there should be a flee escalation. the ones that I'm purposely\nthrowing you head first into some big guy because you have to do that to\ncomplete or progress a mission or a storyline \u2014 I don't think there should be\na progression on those, only on the randoms. I want the rest of the world to\nbe dangerous\u2026 if you step into danger level 3 you're going to see some big bad\nguys and there is a chance you're going to get stuck having that fight that\nmight end the game for you.\"\n\nHis own log is the measurement behind it: he flees everything at ~100 HP or\nmore on random ground and wins the escape roll nearly every time. OTA-1009\nmade the flee contested (fastest pursuer's d20 + speed) and OTA-1459 made it\ncost stamina, and neither moved the outcome \u2014 the bar was the same on the\nfirst break as on the fourth, on a danger-1 verge as in a danger-5 pit, for a\nrat as for a Legendary.\n\nON RANDOM GROUND THE PURSUER'S BAR NOW MOVES\n  +1 per danger level above 1 (danger 3 \u2192 +2, danger 5 \u2192 +4)\n  +0 / +1 / +2 / +3 by the pursuer's rarity\n  +2 per failed break THIS encounter (2nd try +2, 3rd try +4 \u2026)\n  \u22122 when the pursuer is at or under half HP, \u22124 at or under a quarter\nThe one who can catch you is chosen AFTER escalation, so a bleeding sprinter\nloses the chase to a fresh brute. The roll card prints the breakdown (\"Pursuit\n25 \u2014 Mud Wasp (d20 14 + 11: SPD 5, danger +2, Rare +2, 2nd try +2)\"), a failed\nbreak says \"They have your measure now. The next break will be harder.\" before\nthe volley lands, and the FLEE chip carries the exact odds (\"flee 48%\"),\ncounted over all 400 d20 pairs \u2014 from the SAME reader the roll is built from\n(state/fleeOdds), so the chip cannot promise a different chase than the tap\nproduces. His picture at DEX 11 (+1 Reclaimer): danger 3 vs a Rare, 66% \u2192 57%\n\u2192 48% over three tries; danger 5 vs a Legendary on the third try, 30%.\n\nRANDOM IS DECLARED BY THE PRODUCER, NEVER INFERRED\nThere is no field on an Enemy or a scene that says \"this fight is a\nmission's\", and there are dozens of scripted spawn sites against four world\nrolls. So the four rolls stamp `Enemy.unscripted` \u2014 beginScene's encounter,\nthe climb encounter, the rest ambush, the patrol crossing \u2014 and every scripted\nspawn (hunt stages, core guardians, chain marks, captors, summit bosses,\nhostile traders, raids, hostile-ground patrols, and every body from a save\nbefore this OTA) resolves to exactly OTA-1009's escapePursuit, asserted equal.\nA lineup escalates only when EVERY live body carries the mark: a mission mark\nthat joins a roaming pack turns the scene scripted, which is the direction the\nrule leans. The mark rides on the enemy like `pos` and `coating`, so splices,\nsaves and loads carry it with no bookkeeping. The failed-break count lives on\nthe scene (`fleeAttempts`), reset by FRESH_ENEMY_ARRAYS and by every lineup\nproducer, so it cannot outlive the bodies it was earned against.\n\nUnder the OTA-1400 line ratchet, `injectFactionParty` moved verbatim to\napp/state/factionParty.ts (its three callers pass `scalePowerOf` in);\ngameStore is at 36,914 lines.\n\n- app/engine/fleeEscalation.ts (NEW) \u2014 the mark, the four terms, the escalated\n  pursuit, the exact odds.\n- app/state/fleeOdds.ts (NEW) \u2014 the one reader for the bar: the dispatch and\n  the FLEE chip both go through it.\n- app/state/factionParty.ts (NEW) \u2014 injectFactionParty, moved.\n- app/engine/types.ts \u2014 Enemy.unscripted. app/engine/combatRules.ts \u2014\n  EscapePursuit.note, printed on the card.\n- app/state/gameStore.ts \u2014 four producers stamp; the dispatch reads\n  fleePursuitFor; the failed-escape arm counts and speaks; CurrentScene\n  .fleeAttempts; FRESH_ENEMY_ARRAYS resets it.\n- app/components/InputBox.tsx \u2014 \"flee 48%\".\n- __tests__/ota1678TheChaseGetsHarder.test.ts \u2014 25 tests, including the\n  scripted-lineup identity with escapePursuit, the bestiary-wide worst case,\n  and the producer census (exactly four stamps, no scripted site touches it).\n- __tests__/ota1009, ota1116, ota1015, ota1035, ota1159, ota1321, ota1476,\n  ota1506 \u2014 pins repointed to the shared reader, the moved spawner, and the\n  odds-bearing FLEE label; their claims are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LGFtzR6AQJbu4XdR28y3fX",
